# Authoring floor — BML + cached native

**Floor:** high-grammar BML (or higher) with the optimal cached native speed compiler (`.fkb` / `.dylib`).

**Wrong shape:** `*-xtal.fk` — local disposable bridge at best, never committed ice, never the floor.

Door: `AGENTS.md`. Mirror: `./fkwu observe/authoring-altitude-run.fk`.  
Witness: `./fkwu form/form-stdlib/tests/form-cli-author-high-band.fk` → 4095.  
Picture: `form/form-stdlib/bml/form-cli-author-high.bml`.  
North star: `grammars/bml-native-north-star.form`.

## Prefer

- Authority in `form/form-stdlib/bml/*.bml`
- Executable `section [form.bml]` / `section [form.lift]`
- Fresh native cache (`.fkb`, `.dylib` when emission sits)
- Proof bands

## Don't treat as the floor

- `*-xtal.fk` crystallizations (gitignored local cache only)
- Growing `runtime/fkwu-uni.c` for new runtime meaning

## Organs

Existing `.fk` organs remain welcome. Name any forced lowering as the next BML+native-cache door.
